  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A campsite 5 minutes south of Grasse, the perfume capital, at 150 m altitude and 15 kilometres from Cannes, according to its official website. A good compromise for those who want to enjoy the hinterland while staying close to the coast.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The Pays de Grasse tourist office ticks "pets welcome" and "pets accepted in the accommodations". Neither the campsite nor the tourist office publishes a dog surcharge or any limit on number or size. Calling before booking lets you find out the precise terms (size, breed, rate).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the campsite is close to a golf course and a shopping centre — handy for errands, but remember to ask for a shaded pitch for the hot summer days.</div>

      <h2>With your dog: what to know</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://www.campinglapaoute.com/">campsite's official website</a> publishes no rule on animals. The <a href="https://www.paysdegrassetourisme.fr/en/camping-la-paoute-919071/">Pays de Grasse tourist office</a> page ticks both "pets welcome" and "<strong>pets accepted in accommodation</strong>": your dog can therefore come on a pitch as well as in rental accommodation.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Surcharge</strong>: not published by the campsite or the tourist office. Have it confirmed when booking.</li>
        <li><strong>Setting</strong>: pitches separated by hedges and shaded by olive trees several centuries old; grounds closed at night according to the tourist office.</li>
        <li><strong>Opening</strong>: all year round according to the tourist office, with a swimming pool from mid-May to end of September; the snack bar opens from 1 June to 15 September according to the campsite website, from 15 June to 15 September according to the tourist office.</li>
        <li><strong>Not specified by the establishment</strong>: number of dogs, maximum size, possible refusal of category 1 and 2 dogs, dog left alone at the campsite, pool access, documents requested, leash requirement.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>With a dog, the shade of the olive trees is a real asset in summer on the Riviera. And if you're looking for an activity to share nearby, the <a href="/en/fiche-activite-club-canin-grasse">Grasse dog club</a> offers agility and training.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: put your vaccination booklet in the glove box, even if the campsite does not mention it, you may be asked for it at reception.</div>

      <h2>Worth checking before you book</h2>
      <p>The official website presents pitches separated by hedges with individual hook-ups, a sanitary block and individual bathrooms (one for people with reduced mobility), and a shopping centre nearby (100 m) and an international 18-hole golf course. Dog surcharge and conditions (number, size, categories) to be confirmed by phone on 04 93 09 11 42.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The official website places the campsite 5 minutes south of Grasse, 15 kilometres from Cannes and its sandy beaches, and 20 minutes from Lake Saint-Cassien. Dog rules on the beaches and at the lake should be checked with the local councils.</p>
    </div>

